Subject: midimap: name the MIDI mapper the way Windows does

midiOutGetDevCaps on MIDI_MAPPER gave "Wine midi mapper", which music
programs show as the first MIDI output (FL Studio's MIDI settings list
it at the top). Windows calls it "Microsoft MIDI Mapper", which is also
what FL Studio already prints in its description column.
---
diff --git a/dlls/midimap/midimap.c b/dlls/midimap/midimap.c
--- a/dlls/midimap/midimap.c
+++ b/dlls/midimap/midimap.c
@@ -506,7 +506,7 @@
 {
     static const MIDIOUTCAPSW mappercaps = {
 	0x00FF, 0x0001, 0x0100, /* Manufacturer and Product ID */
-        L"Wine midi mapper", MOD_MAPPER, 0, 0, 0xFFFF,
+        L"Microsoft MIDI Mapper", MOD_MAPPER, 0, 0, 0xFFFF,
 	/* Native returns volume caps of underlying device + MIDICAPS_STREAM */
 	MIDICAPS_VOLUME|MIDICAPS_LRVOLUME
     };
